  "releaseNotes": "v0.5.0 (2025-10-25):\n\n            BREAKING CHANGES:\n            - Migrated from .NET Core 3.1 to .NET 9.0\n            - Namespace reorganization (Modes/, Hardware/, Interop/)\n            - Project restructured into src/ and samples/ directories\n            - Modernized value types (Frequency, DeviceInfo, CrystalFrequency)\n\n            NEW FEATURES:\n            - Windows support in native library resolver\n            - IComparable support for Frequency type\n            - Improved frequency arithmetic with overflow protection\n            - Source Link support for debugging NuGet packages\n            - Comprehensive .editorconfig with 60+ code quality rules\n            - Performance analyzers (CA1827, CA1829, CA1841, CA1851)\n            - Security analyzers for P/Invoke (CA2101, CA3075, CA5350, CA5351)\n            - Standard exception constructors for all custom exceptions\n            - Input validation with proper exception types\n\n            IMPROVEMENTS:\n            - Replaced DllImport with LibraryImport for better performance\n            - Implemented proper dispose pattern with managed/unmanaged separation\n            - Added comprehensive XML documentation\n            - Cross-platform build support (LF line endings)\n            - Build scripts (build.sh, runsample.sh)\n\n            FIXES:\n            - Proper resource disposal in async samples\n            - Clear error messages for invalid device indices\n            - Finalizer no longer accesses disposed managed resources\n\n            See CHANGELOG.md for complete details and upgrade guide.",
